  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let \\(f(x)=\\frac{1}{\\log |x|}\\)\nThe points of disconinuity of \\(f(x)\\) are those points where \\(f(x)\\) is undefined or infinite. It is undefined when \\(x=0\\) and is infinite when \\(\\log |x|=0,|x|=1\\), i.e. \\(x= \\pm 1\\).\n\\(\\therefore \\quad\\) Set of points of discontinuity \\(=\\{-1,0,1\\}\\).",
    "image": null
  },
